From b91d2e52c705ab1cfa3d0bf8c5860cfa2b4c446f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:21:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verifier V26: replay the single-lot custody instructions
 through the kernel [skip ci]

V26:custody-replay (custody seasons): each landed transaction with one
custody instruction among OpenLot, SetLotQuota, SetLotOrder,
RevokeLotOrder, ConsumeLot and CloseLot is run through
permutation_rules::frontier::custody on the states recorded before it,
with the program's account order and argument reading
(permutation-frontier/src/proc/custody.rs) and the wallet prologue's
signer (the Citizen's wallet, or its unexpired session). A kernel
refusal or a result other than what the transaction left in the lot
(and, where the program writes them, the vault's custody counts) is a
FAIL, CustodyReplayMismatch. Missing evidence, the caravan instructions
and several custody instructions in one transaction are UNVERIFIABLE,
CustodyReplayIncomplete. The guard's traces stay, so a custody season
is still never a PASS.

Tests (tests/custody_replay.rs, no key generated, derived or used to
sign): the kernel's own results replay to a match; a unit off, the
vault's counts off, a refused signer, an expired session, a refusal
(more than the order, a stale nonce, closing a lot with goods, a wrong
rent account) are mismatches; missing states are not FAILs; random
kernel runs; and through verify() with the instruction put into a
recorded transaction's message without signing it again.

